# Renders are derived and deterministic (fixed seeds, no clock input), so the
# same commit always rebuilds the same bytes — see dendrite-tux/README.md.
# The preview JPEGs are the exception: they are what each README shows.
#
# Every pattern is written `**/build/…`, not `build/…`. A pattern containing a
# slash anywhere but the end is ANCHORED to the directory holding this file, so
# a bare `build/*` here would only ever match `synapse-wallpapers/build/*` and
# would miss `dendrite-tux/build/`, one level down. `**/` restores the
# match-at-any-depth behaviour that the repo-root `build/` line has.
#
# The three lines are ordered, and none is redundant:
#   !**/build/           the repo-root .gitignore excludes `build/` as a
#                        DIRECTORY, and git does not descend into an excluded
#                        directory — without this the negation below is
#                        unreachable.
#   **/build/*           exclude the contents (not the directory), which keeps
#                        that negation eligible.
#   !**/build/*-preview.jpg   re-include the previews.
!**/build/
**/build/*
!**/build/*-preview.jpg
